 "notes": "Wouters & Brun (2013), Chandra X-ray spectrum of Hydra A: 95% CL exclusion on g_gamma-a from absence of photon-ALP oscillation irregularities. Curve digitised from the vector path in fig4.eps of the arXiv e-print (ROOT-generated), axes calibrated from log-scale tick marks; flat level 8.30e-12 GeV^-1 matches the quoted g < 8.3e-12 GeV^-1 for m_a < 7e-12 eV. This is the paper's headline conservative magnetic-field-profile limit (the 'more likely' profile would give 4.3e-12, not plotted). Astrophysical conversion limit: no dark-matter density assumption, no rescaling applied. Figure spans m_a = 1e-12 to 1.4e-11 eV; the limit is mass-independent below the plotted range (m_a << m_gamma).",
